# Definition of Done (DoD) — {{device_name}}

The **universal completion bar** every story / backlog item must clear **in addition to its own
acceptance criteria**. Enforces IEC 62304 / ISO 13485 / QMS discipline at each increment.
A story is **Done** only when **all applicable items** are satisfied and evidenced.

> Three V&V layers: **measurable benefit** → test *objective* · **acceptance criteria** → test *cases* ·
> **DoD** → universal *exit gate*

_"Applicable" = an item that touches the area. Items that don't apply are marked N/A with a one-line reason._

## 1. Functional & acceptance

- [ ] All of the story's **acceptance criteria pass** (automated where possible).
- [ ] The story's **measurable benefit is demonstrably met** (the metric in the "so that" is evidenced).
- [ ] Behavior matches the PRD/architecture; no scope drift.

## 2. Code quality

- [ ] Built to **architecture patterns** — ports & adapters, results-not-exceptions, consistent naming.
- [ ] **No PHI in logs / exceptions**; structured logging with correlation / provenance ID.
- [ ] **Peer code review approved**; no unresolved review comments.

## 3. Tests & verification

- [ ] **Unit + integration tests green**; full suite passes (no regressions).
- [ ] Each new/changed test carries **`@Traces("FR..","RISK..")`** (or equivalent traceability annotation)
  linking it to the requirement / risk it verifies.
- [ ] A **fake / stub exists for every port** introduced; **Testcontainers** (or equivalent) for real-DB paths.
- [ ] **Test coverage of new/changed code meets the threshold:**
  - **General code:** ≥ 80% line and ≥ 70% branch (new/changed).
  - **Safety-relevant code** (anything traced to a `RISK-*` or a safety predicate):
    ≥ 95% branch AND 100% of identified safety scenarios covered by an explicit traced test.
  - Uncovered safety-relevant branches require a documented justification (coverage-gap analysis).

## 4. Safety, risk & traceability (regulated — IEC 62304 Class {{iec62304_class}})

- [ ] **Requirement traceability updated** (FR → design → test) via traceability annotation or matrix.
- [ ] **Risk controls verified**; if the work surfaced a new hazard, `risk-management-file.md` /
  `risk-register.md` + `open-items.md` are updated.
- [ ] **Chain-of-custody / audit trail** emitted where the story transforms or accesses clinical data.

## 5. Security & supply chain

- [ ] **No unauthorized SOUP** — any new dependency authorized and added to `soup-register.md`.
- [ ] **SBOM regenerated** and reviewed; no unresolved high/critical vulnerability.
- [ ] Secrets via the secrets provider port — **no secrets in code or logs**.
- [ ] For parser/connector-touching stories: basic untrusted-input safety (size/time limits, validation).

## 6. Data & privacy

- [ ] PHI **encrypted in transit and at rest**; data-minimization respected.
- [ ] **No real PHI in tests** — de-identified/synthetic fixtures only.

_(Applicable only when `phi_handling = {{phi_handling}}`.)_

## 7. Build, CI & documentation (DHF)

- [ ] **CI green**; build reproducible; dependencies resolve only from `{{artifact_repo}}`.
- [ ] **ADR added/updated** if a design decision changed; affected QMS docs updated.
- [ ] `open-items.md` updated (closed/added as needed).
- [ ] Commit references the **story ID + FR/RISK**; pushed to `{{source_control}}`.

## Roles & sign-off [QMS]

Developer self-verifies the DoD; reviewer confirms.
Formal roles, records, and the review SOP are to be established in the ISO 13485 QMS.
Until then, DoD verification is recorded in the PR/commit.
